<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
     AresLauncher - the remove affordance shown on every home item while the grid is in edit mode.

     Tapping it takes the item off the HOME SCREEN. It does not uninstall the app: iOS conflates
     those two, a launcher must not. Uninstall stays in the long-press context popup, where it has
     a confirmation step and where the user already expects to find it.

     ## Why the visible badge is smaller than the view that hosts it

     The first cut painted the backdrop as the ImageView's background, so the circle filled the
     whole 48dp touch target. On a 1x1 tile that is nearly as wide as the app icon itself, and
     because the icon is centred in its cell while the badge is pinned to the corner, the two barely
     overlapped: it read as a detached blob floating beside the icon rather than a badge on it. The
     user asked for "a little x", and that was not little.

     Both sizes are wanted independently. The touch target has to clear the 44dp minimum; the glyph
     has to stay small enough not to bury what it sits on. So the target stays 48dp and the drawn
     badge is composed here at its own size, centred. AresRemoveBadge sets scaleType=CENTER so this
     draws at its intrinsic size instead of being stretched to fill.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <item
        android:width="@dimen/ares_remove_badge_size"
        android:height="@dimen/ares_remove_badge_size"
        android:gravity="center">
        <shape android:shape="oval">
            <solid android:color="@color/ares_my_icon_button_container" />
        </shape>
    </item>

    <item
        android:width="@dimen/ares_remove_badge_glyph_size"
        android:height="@dimen/ares_remove_badge_glyph_size"
        android:drawable="@drawable/ares_remove_badge_glyph"
        android:gravity="center" />
</layer-list>
